2. TASKS
──────────────────────────────

Below is the table of tasks. Note that tasks with fallback behavior have sub-tasks defined (AT4, AT7, and AT8 include children tasks for handling error/fallback conditions).

| Name                           | Text                                                                                                                                         | Relation | Location                         | Number of Robots | Justification                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |
|--------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|----------------------------------|------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| **AT1: Navigate to Storage**   | Navigate to the designated storage location to access the required resources.                                                                | AND      | Storage Location                 | 1                | A single robot can navigate to a specific storage location.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |
| **AT2: Request Resource**      | Send a message to the storage with the precise specification of the requested resources.                                                     | AND      | Storage Location                 | 1                | The robot must communicate with the storage to request the resource; one robot is sufficient for this task.                                                                                                                                                                                             |
| **AT3: Wait for Retrieval**    | Wait at the storage until the resources have been retrieved.                                                                                | AND      | Storage Location                 | 1                | The robot remains at the storage location until the resources are ready, ensuring the collection process is completed.                                                                                                                                                                                   |
| **AT4: Battery Check in Collection** | Monitor battery level during collection and handle low battery condition if it falls below 10%.                                          | AND      | Storage Location / Recharging Station | 1                | This task ensures safe operation during collection. Its runtime uses a fallback: if the battery is sufficient (AT4.1), continue collection; if not, fallback to returning to the recharging station (AT4.2).                                                                                                         |
| **AT4.1: Continue Collection** | Proceed with resource collection as normal.                                                                                                 | AND      | Storage Location                 | 1                | This sub-task executes if the battery level is adequate.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |
| **AT4.2: Recharge and Reassign Mission** | Return to the recharging station and assign the remaining collection task to another robot.                                                | AND      | Recharging Station              | 1                | This fallback action is triggered when the battery level drops below 10%, ensuring that the mission is not halted due to power failure.                                                                                                                                                               |
| **AT5: Navigate to Delivery Location** | Navigate to the specified delivery location to deliver the collected resources.                                                               | AND      | Specified Delivery Location      | 1                | A single robot can navigate to the delivery location.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |
| **AT6: Deliver Resource**      | Deliver the collected resource to the specified location or checkpoint.                                                                      | AND      | Specified Delivery Location / Checkpoint | 1                | The delivery action is performed by one robot to ensure the resource reaches its destination.                                                                                                                                                                                                         |
| **AT7: Battery Check in Delivery** | Monitor battery level during delivery and handle low battery condition if it falls below 30%.                                               | AND      | Delivery Location / Checkpoint   | 1                | This task ensures safe operation during delivery. Its runtime uses a fallback: if battery is adequate (AT7.1), continue delivery; otherwise, fallback to returning the resource to a checkpoint (AT7.2).                                                                                                  |
| **AT7.1: Proceed with Delivery** | Continue with the resource delivery process normally.                                                                                        | AND      | Delivery Location                | 1                | This sub-task is executed if the battery level is sufficient during delivery.                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |
| **AT7.2: Return Resource and Reassign Delivery** | Return the resource to a checkpoint and assign the remaining delivery task to another robot.                                                 | AND      | Checkpoint                      | 1                | This fallback action is triggered when the battery level drops below 30% during delivery, ensuring that the resource is safeguarded and the mission continues.                                                                                                                                     |
